  "bundle": [
    {
      "path": "cordis.patch.yml",
      "text": "# dsh-debug-mode composition overlay: mounts the host controller and the\n# browser debug toggle. The loader refuses to replace a row with a different\n# package name, so the official ui-plan Plan chip stays and our control rides\n# the composer's conversation.input.left list seat next to it. Exclusivity is\n# enforced host-side: /debug turns plan mode off, and selecting Debug from the\n# toggle turns plan mode off first.\n- insert:\n    - id: debug-mode\n      name: 'dsh-debug-mode/host'\n      config:\n        section: |-\n          You are in debug mode. Debug mode authorizes instrumenting or pausing the project to obtain runtime evidence:\n          - Locate the smallest relevant code range with searches, LSP, and file reads before changing anything.\n          - Frontend targets: use the default listener transport. It starts a run-owned collector, saves bounded sanitized events to the local trace.jsonl file, and exposes them through debug_control. Ask the user to reproduce, then read the persisted evidence.\n          - Use local-log only when the user explicitly requests console/terminal-only output; it does not start a collector or create a trace file.\n          - Backend targets: start the debugger with breakpoints in the located statements, then ask the user to reproduce.\n          - Diagnose from runtime evidence first; propose a fix only after reporting the root cause, evidence, and confidence.\n          - Fixes require user choice before editing; verify a fix by re-running the same reproduction.\n          - debug_finish removes probes, trace runtime files, platform configuration, any listener that was actually started, and debug processes.\n    - id: debug-mode-client\n      name: 'dsh-debug-mode'\n"
    }
  ],
